216:\begin{abstract}
217-We consider a set $SPG(\caA)$ of
218:pure split states on a quantum spin chain $\caA$
219:which are invariant under the on-site action $\tau$ of a finite group $G$
220-.
221:For each element $\omega$ in $SPG(\caA)$ we can associate a second cohomology 
222- class $c_{\omega,R}$
223-of $G$. 
224:We consider a classification of $SPG(\caA)$ whose criterion is given as follows:
225-$\omega_{0}$ and $\omega_{1}$ in  $SPG(\caA)$
226:are equivalent if there are automorphisms $\Xi_{R}$, $\Xi_L$ on 
227-$\caA_{R}$, $\caA_{L}$ (right and left half infinite chains) preserving the symmetry $\tau$, such that
228-$\omega_{1}$ and $\omega_{0}\circ\lmk \Xi_{L}\otimes \Xi_{R}\rmk$
229:are quasi-equivalent.
230-It means that we can 
231-move $\omega_{0}$
232-close to $\omega_{1}$
233-without changing the entanglement nor breaking the symmetry.
234:We show that the second cohomology class $c_{\omega,R}$
235:is the complete invariant of this classification.
236-
