367-\begin{abstract}
368-We consider the classification problem of 
369-symmetry protected topological (SPT) phases on quantum spin systems.
370:SPT phases are gapped short-range-entangled quantum phases with a symmetry $G$.
371-We explain that in one and two-dimensional quantum spin systems, 
372:there are $H^{2}(G, U(1))$/ $H^{3}(G, U(1))$-valued invariant, confirming
373-a physicists conjecture.
374-\end{abstract}
