381-instead of $\omega$.
382-Of course we do have an action of the symmetry on the GNS triple
383-$(\caH,\pi,\Omega)$ of $\omega$.
384-But this action is given by a genuine unitary action $U$. It does not
385-give any nontrivial cohomology class.
386-One may argue that we still can investigate this genuine unitary representation $U$
387:as an invariant, like by investigating which irreducible representation is included in it. 
388-But in the paper \cite{OGS}, we show  that at least for
389:on-site linear action of finite group, {\it every} irreducible representation is contained
390-in $U$.
391-Because of this result, we do not expect that $U$ can play an important role in
392-the classification problem of SPT-phases.
393-We also would like to remark that importance of the cut is not specialized 
394-to our theory.
395-It is actually in the sprit of the original paper \cite{po} \cite{po2},
396-and of all the works considering the entanglement entropy. 
397:In the index theory of \cite{bdf}, it is also
398-very important to consider the half of the system.
