   709	{\new{
   710	The non-trivial index implies a lower bound of the entanglement entropy.
   711	The entanglement entropy in our setting is defined as follows.
   712	Let $(\caH_{\varphi_R},\pi_{\varphi_R},\Omega_{\varphi_R})$, 
   713	$\caK_\varphi$, $\iota_\varphi$, $J_{\varphi}$
   714	be as in Theorem \ref{sp}.
   715	Then there exists a density matrix $\rho$ on $\caK_\varphi$ such that
   716	$\left. \omega\right\vert_{\caA_R}=\Tr_{\caK_\varphi}\lmk
   717	\rho\iota_\varphi\circ \pi_{\varphi_R}\lmk \cdot\rmk\rmk$.
   718	The entanglement entropy of $\varphi$ is the von Neumann entropy 
   719	of $\rho$.
   720	By the time reversal invariance of the system, we have
