393:\subsection{Projective representations of $G$}\label{pp}
394-A map $\sigma : G\times G\to \bbT$ is called a $2$-cocycle of $G$ if 
395-\begin{enumerate}
396-\item
397-$\sigma(g,h)\sigma(gh,k)=\sigma(h,k)\sigma(g,hk)$, for all $g,h,k\in G$,
398-\item 
399-$\sigma(g,e)=\sigma(e,g)=1$ for all $g\in G$.
