426- such that $\uu(g)\uu(h) = \sigma(g, h)\uu(gh)$ for all $g,h\in G$. Note that we get $\uu(e)=\unit_{\caH}$ from the latter condition.
427- We call $\sigma$, the $2$-cocycle of $G$ associated to $V$, and call
428: $[\sigma]_{H^{2}(G,\bbT)}$ the second cohomology class of $G$
429: associated to $V$. We occasionally say $(\caH,V)$ is a projective unitary representation with $2$-cocycle $\sigma$.
430:The character of  a finite dimensional projective unitary representation $(\caH,V,\sigma)$
431-is given by $\chi_{V}(g)=\Tr_{\caH}V(g)$, for $g\in G$.
