321-$\caA_\Lambda$. By considering a differential equation satisfied by the spectral projection $P_s(\Lambda)$ of the Hamiltonian $H_s(\Lambda)$ corresponding
322:to the lowest eigenvalue, we may explicitly define in this case the automorphisms connecting the ground state spaces. 
323-In contrast, for infinite systems, we do not have a Hamiltonian $H_s$ in the $C^*$-algebra of quantum spin systems. Of course we can consider the bulk Hamiltonian $H_s$, but $H_s$ depends on the GNS representation, and the meaning of $\frac{d}{ds} H_s$ is ambiguous. Therefore, we have to find an alternative way to prove our adiabatic theorem. 
