319:Let us specify what we mean by a \emph{gapped}  Hamiltonian:
320-\begin{defn}
321-A Hamiltonian $H:=\left(H_\Lambda\right)_{\Lambda\in{\mathfrak I}_{\bbZ}}$
322:associated with a positive translation invariant finite range interaction is \emph{gapped}  
323-if there exists $\gamma>0$ and $N_0\in\nan$ 
324-such that the difference 
325-between the smallest and the next-smallest eigenvalue of $H_\Lambda$, is bounded below by 
326-$\gamma$,  for all finite intervals $\Lambda\subset\bbZ$ with $|\Lambda|\ge N_0$. 
327-\end{defn}
328-We call this $\gamma$ a gap of the Hamiltonian $H$.
329-Note that the lowest eigenvalue may be degenerate.
