372-Let $\caD_N$ be a subspace of $\otimes_{i=0}^{N-1}\cc^n$, for each $N\in \nan$.
373-We say that the sequence of subspaces $\{\caD_N\}_{N\in \nan}$ satisfies the {\it intersection property},
374-if there exists an $m\in\nan$, such that the relation 
375-\begin{equation}\label{intersection property}
376-\caD_N = \bigcap_{x=0}^{N-m} (\bbC^{n})^{\otimes x}\otimes \caD_{m}\otimes (\bbC^{n})^{\otimes N-m-x}, 
377-\end{equation} holds for all $N\ge m$.
378-In order to specify the number $m\in \nan$, we will say that $\{\caD_N\}_{N\in\nan}$ satisfies  Property~(I,$m$) 
379-when (\ref{intersection property}) holds for $m$
380-and all $N\ge m$.
381-Note that Property~(I,$m$) implies Property~(I,$m'$)  for all $m'\ge m$.
382-
