390-\tau_x\lmk Q_m\rmk, & \text{if }  X=[x,x+m-1]  \text{ for some }  x\in\bbZ\\
391-0,&\text{otherwise}
392-\end{cases}\,.
393-\end{align*}
394-By (\ref{intersection property}), we see that $\ker H_{[0,N-1]}=\caD_N$,
395-for $N\ge m$, for the Hamiltonian $H=(H_{\Lambda})$ associated with $\Phi$.
396:We shall refer to that particular Hamiltonian as the \emph{parent Hamiltonian}
397-of $\{\caD_N\}$.
