356:Let us specify what we mean by gapped Hamiltonian in this paper.
357-\begin{defn}
358-A Hamiltonian $H:=\left(H_\Lambda\right)_{\Lambda\in{\mathfrak I}}$
359:associated with a positive translation invariant finite range interaction is \emph{gapped}  
360-if there exists $\gamma>0$ and $N_0\in\nan$ 
361-such that the difference 
362-between the smallest and the next-smallest eigenvalue of $H_\Lambda$, is bounded below by 
