368:Now we introduce the $C^1$-classification of gapped Hamiltonians with $\beta_U$-symmetry.
369-We say  $\Phi:[0,1]\ni t\mapsto\Phi(t)\in  {\caJ}$ 
370:is a continuous and piecewise $C^1$-path if  for each $X\in{\mathfrak S}$, the path
371:$[0,1]\ni t\mapsto \Phi(t;X)\in {\caA}_X$ is continuous and piecewise $C^1$
372-with respect to the norm topology.
373:\begin{defn}[$C^1$-classification of gapped Hamiltonians with symmetry]\label{def:phasec}
374-Let $U:G\to \caU_n$ be a unitary representation of a group $G$ on $\bbC^n$.
375:Let $H_0,H_1$ be gapped  Hamiltonians associated with $\beta_U$-invariant interactions
376-$\Phi_{0},\Phi_{1}\in{\caJ}$.
377-We say that  $H_0,H_1$ are
378:$C^1$-equivalent with $\beta_U$-symmetry if the following conditions are satisfied.
379-\begin{enumerate}
380:\item There exists $m\in\nan$ and a continuous and piecewise $C^1$-path $\Phi:[0,1]\to {\caJ}_m$ such that $\Phi(0)=\Phi_0$, 
381-$\Phi(1)= \Phi_1$.
382-\item  Let   $H(t)$ be the Hamiltonian associated with $\Phi(t)$ for each $t\in[0,1]$.
383-There are $\gamma>0$, $N_0\in\nan$, and finite intervals $I(t)=[a(t), b(t)]$, whose endpoints $a(t), b(t)$ smoothly depending on $t\in[0,1]$,
384-such that for all finite intervals $\Lambda\subset\bbZ$ with $|\Lambda|\ge N_0$,
385-the smallest eigenvalue of $H(t)_\Lambda$ is in $I(t)$ and
386-the rest of the spectrum is in $[b(t)+\gamma,\infty)$.
387-\item
388-For each $t\in[0,1]$, $\Phi(t)$ is $\beta_U$-invariant.
389-\end{enumerate}
390-\end{defn}
391-\begin{rem}
392:We write $H_0\simeq_{C^1,U} H_1$ when
393-$H_0,H_1$ are 
394:$C^1$-equivalent with $\beta_U$-symmetry.
395:If furthermore the path  $\Phi(t)$ can be taken in ${\caJ}_m$ we write
396:$H_0\simeq_{C^1,U,m}H_1$.
