629-\section{Outline of the argument}
630-\label{s:outlie}
631-
632:Before discussing the settings and results in detail, we recall the notions of projective representations of a symmetry group and the corresponding second group cohomology, and also give an informal account of the proofs of the main results.
633-
634:\paragraph*{Projective representations and degree-2 cohomology classes}
635:Let $G$ be a finite group that describes on-site symmetry of the spin system.
636-We fix a homomorphism $\ua:G\to\{1,-1\}$,
637-which gives a decomposition\footnote{%
638-This decomposition  is known as a UA-decomposition.
639-See, e.g., \cite{Par,LS}. 
640-The same structure is also known as a Real structure on a group following Atiyah;
641-see, e.g., \cite[Chapter 2]{BG}.
642-} $G=G^+\sqcup G^-$ with $G^\pm\coloneqq\{g\in G\mid\ua(g)=\pm1\}$.
643-In the following we always consider the pair $(G,\ua)$ as the basic data
644-and denote it simply by $G$, leaving $\ua$ implicit.
645-In the main part of the paper, we assume $G$ is finite,
646:but we can generalize our theorems to compact Lie groups.
647-We will give a brief discussion on this generalized case in Appendix~\ref{app:Lie}.
