1481:\paragraph{Comment on the case $G=U(1)$}
1482:Our approach does not say anything nontrivial when $G=U(1)$, since $H^2(U(1),\Uo)=\{0\}$ when defined using the Borel functions.
1483:This is unfortunate, since early extensions of the original theorem of LSM were mainly about relaxing the $SO(3)$ symmetry to its $U(1)$ subgroup. 
1484:One important result in this direction was obtained in \cite{OYA}, where it was shown that there is no unique gapped ground state if the filling factor $\nu$ of a $U(1)$-symmetric system is not an integer. 
