329-\section{Setting and main results}
330-We start by summarizing standard setup of quantum spin chains on the infinite chain \cite{BR1,BR2}.
331-Let $S$ be an element of $\frac 12 \bbN$ and let $\SSS=\{-S,-S+1,\ldots,S-1,S\}$.
332-We denote the algebra of $(2S+1)\times (2S+1)$ matrices by $\Mat_{2S+1}$.
--
348-Note that $\caA_{\Lambda}$ for $\Lambda\in {\mathfrak S}_{\bbZ}$,
349-and $\caA_R$ can be regarded naturally as subalgebras of
350-$\caA$.
351-Under this identification, for each $z\in \bbZ$,
352-we denote the 
353-spin operators in $\caA_{\{z\}}\subset\caA$ by $\hS_{1}^{(z)}, \hS_{2}^{(z)}, \hS_{3}^{(z)}$.
354-We denote the set of local observables by $\caA_{\rm loc}=\bigcup_{\Lambda\in{\mathfrak S}_\bbZ}\caA_{\Lambda}
355-$.
356:We denote by $\tau_x$ the automorphisms on $\caA$ representing the space translation by  $x\in\bbZ$.
357-
358-A mathematical model of a quantum spin chain is fully specified by its interaction $\Phi$.
359-An interaction is a map $\Phi$ from 
360-${\mathfrak S}_{\bbZ}$ into ${\caA}_{\rm loc}$ such
361-that $\Phi(X) \in {\caA}_{X}$ 
362-and $\Phi(X) = \Phi(X)^*$
363-for $X \in {\mathfrak S}_{\bbZ}$. 
364:An interaction $\Phi$ is translation invariant if
365-$\Phi(X+x)=\tau_x(\Phi(X))$, 
366-for all $x\in{\mathbb Z}$ and $X\in  {\mathfrak S}_{\bbZ}$, and  is of finite range if there exists  $m\in {\mathbb N}$ such that
367-$\Phi(X)=0$ for $X$ with diameter larger than $m$.
368-For an interaction $\Phi$ and a finite set $\Lambda\in{\mathfrak S}_{\bbZ}$, we define the local Hamiltonian
369-as
370-\begin{equation}\label{GenHamiltonian}
371-\lmk H_{\Phi}\rmk_{\Lambda}:=\sum_{X\subset{\Lambda}}\Phi(X).
372-\end{equation}
