396:The following definition clarifies what we mean by a model with a unique gapped ground state.
397-See \cite{BR2} for the general theory.
398-\begin{defn}
399:We say that a model with an interaction $\Phi$ has a unique gapped ground state if 
400:(i)~the $\alpha^\Phi$-ground state, which we denote as $\varphi$, is unique, and 
401-(ii)~there exists $\gamma>0$ such that
402-$\sigma(H_{\varphi,\Phi})\setminus\{0\}\subset [\gamma,\infty)$, where  $\sigma(H_{\varphi,\Phi})$ is the spectrum of $H_{\varphi,\Phi}$.
403-\end{defn}
404:Note that the uniqueness of $\varphi$ implies that 0 is a non-degenerate eigenvalue of $H_{\varphi,\Phi}$.
405-
406-We now introduce two types of symmetry relevant to the present study.
407:Time-reversal is the unique  antilinear unital \mbox{$*$-automorphism} $\Xi$ on $\caA$ satisfying
408-\begin{align}
409-\Xi(S_j^{z}) = -S_j^{(z)},\quad j=1,2,3,\quad z\in\bbZ.
410-\end{align}
411-(See Appendix \ref{TR} for the existence of such an automorphism.)
412-For a state $\omega$ on $\caA$, its time-reversal $\hat \omega$ is
413-given by 
414-\begin{equation}
415-\hat \omega(A)
416-=\omega(\Xi(A^*)),\quad
417-A\in \caA.
418-\end{equation}
419-We say $\omega$ is time-reversal invariant if $\omega=\hat\omega$.
420-
421-We also introduce the $\bbZ_2\times\bbZ_2$ symmetry.
422:Let $R_j$ with $j=1,2,3$ be the unique set of unital \mbox{$*$-automorphisms} on $\caA$ satisfying
423-\begin{equation}
424-R_j\bigl(\hS_k^{(z)}\bigr)  
425-=
426-\left\{
427-\begin{gathered}
428-\hS_k^{(z)},\quad j=k\\
429--\hS_{k}^{(z)},\quad j\neq k.
430-\end{gathered} 
431-\right.,\quad \quad j,k=1,2,3,
432-\end{equation}
433-for each $z\in \bbZ$.
434-Note that $R_j$ is essentially the global spin rotation by $\pi$ about the $j$-axis.
435-
436-An interaction $\Phi$ is said to be time-reversal invariant
437-if $\Xi(\Phi(X))=\Phi(X)$
438-for all $X\in {\mathfrak S}_\bbZ$.
439:If $\omega$ is an \mbox{$\alpha^{\Phi}$-ground} state of a translation and time-reversal invariant finite range interaction $\Phi$,
