441-$\hat \omega$ and $\omega\circ\tau_x$ for any $x\in\bbZ$ are also \mbox{$\alpha^{\Phi}$-ground} states.
442:In particular, if $\omega$ is a unique \mbox{$\alpha^{\Phi}$-ground} state, it is pure, time-reversal invariant,  
443:and translation invariant.
444-Similarly, 
445-an interaction $\Phi$ is $\bbZ_2\times\bbZ_2$ invariant if
446- $R_j(\Phi(X))=\Phi(X)$ for $j=1,2$ and
447-for all $X\in {\mathfrak S}_\bbZ$.
448-Note that $\Phi(X)$ automatically satisfies $R_3(\Phi(X))=\Phi(X)$ .
449:If $\omega$ is an \mbox{$\alpha^{\Phi}$-ground} state of a translation and $\bbZ_2\times\bbZ_2$ symmetry invariant finite range interaction $\Phi$,
450-then
451-$\omega\circ R_j$ for $j=1,2,3$ and $\omega\circ\tau_x$ for $x\in\bbZ$ are also \mbox{$\alpha^{\Phi}$-ground} states.
