   909	\section{Indices for half-infinite chains and the proofs of theorems}
   910	\label{s:proof1}
   911	Let us discuss key ingredients of the present work, and prove the theorems and the corollaries.
   912	Throughout the present section, we assume that $\rho$ is a $G$-invariant pure split state.
   913	
   914	\paragraph*{Definition of indices}
   915	We first follow Ogata \cite{OgataZ2}, and define indices $\sigma^\rL_x,\sigma^\rR_x\in\SC$ associated with the state $\rho$ restricted on the half-infinite chains.
   916	See Figure~\ref{f:chain}~(a).
   917	
   918	Let us fix $x\in\bbZ$ and $\rD\in\{\rL,\rR\}$.
   919	Let $\rho^\rD_x$ be the restriction of $\rho$ onto the subalgebra $\AD_x$.
   920	Let $(\calH^\rD_x,\uppi^\rD_x,\Omega^\rD_x)$ be the GNS triple corresponding to $\AD_x$ and $\rho^\rD_x$.
