The first substantive discrepancy is now clear: the literature does not give one uniform compact-\(G\) stability theorem. The general \(H^2\) stability and split-state completeness results are finite-group statements; the compact connected semisimple extension appears in the OTT LSM paper, while the local-symmetry parent-Hamiltonian theorem allows a general group but assumes unitary equivalence of the virtual projective representations. I’m preserving those distinctions in the verified map.
